  "description": "The Bassi03, welded from 7005 aluminum tear-shaped tubing with a 12K carbon fork, is our performance Criterium frame. Whether sprinting on the velodrome, defying the laws of physics during a closed circuit race, or winning an alleycat, the Bassi03 is the frame of choice of Team Bassi. The composite fork with an aluminum steerer, which we chose for its durability, is drilled to accommodate a front brake. The undrilled rear seatstay bridge and the slightly downward sloping top tube are signifiers of the true track identity of the Bassi03.\nMinimal BASSI03 design available in white stripes on matt black mass or gloss black stripes on matt black mass, design created by local design wiz kids Jean-Sebastien Baillat and Guillaume Cardell.\n\nStraight Bladed 12k weave carbon fork with aluminium steer tube\n\nSeat post clamp\n\nDrop-out reinforcement plates and screws\n\n(dimensions in millimeters)",
